Sval: Remove SpecialMessageActions

SpecialMessageActions ran the actions of Firefox's in-app messages. With
the messages removed (remove-messaging.patch), its last callers did one
thing each, which they do directly: the protections panel's info message
opens its link, Firefox View's signed-out Send Tab item opens the account
sign-in page, and a Windows notification that carries messaging relaunch
data is no longer acted on. The module, its schemas, their docs and tests
go, with about:privatebrowsing's remote page access, which only Firefox's
own page used. Targeting.sys.mjs and Logger.sys.mjs stay for Nimbus.

